{
 "schema": "singlet.benchmark.capability",
 "schema_version": "1.0.0",
 "capability": "vdj",
 "title": "V(D)J clonotypes (TCR / BCR)",
 "conclusion": "",
 "methods": "Singlet assembles V(D)J libraries itself (singlet.vdj: segment reference from the GENCODE genome the pipeline uses, 15-mer read classification, per-UMI-consensus junction assembly between codon-checked Cys104 and Phe/Trp118, Cell Ranger barcode and UMI correction). Truth is Cell Ranger vdj's productive high-confidence contigs as published by 10x (pbmc5p_v1: Cell Ranger 3.0.0; pbmc10k_5p_v2: 5.0.0) or by the authors (GSE145370: 3.0.1); Cell Ranger was not re-run. TRUST4 ran on the same FASTQs with 8 threads, its IMGT reference and the 10x whitelist. Metrics are on Cell Ranger's V(D)J cells; V(D)J cells of Singlet and TRUST4 are restricted to the called GEX cells where the dataset has a GEX matrix. V genes that are identical (or 1 nt apart) up to Cys104 count as one (IGKV1-39 / IGKV1D-39 ...). Wrong lineage uses T / B labels from GEX markers (CD3D/E/G, CD2 vs MS4A1, CD79A/B), independent of every V(D)J caller.",
 "status": "draft",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-26T13:30:49+00:00",
 "owner": "vdj-crispr",
